<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="117" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>CI coordination: Bicep-&gt;ARM-JSON pre-compile step for H2a</title>
    <phase>C'' Wave G-1 -- Foundation</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Single additive CI step (az bicep build as a workflow step, output as an artifact), no existing .cs modification. STANDARD per root CLAUDE.md §8.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>One-step, well-specified CI addition -- mechanical, Sonnet @ high.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>waveG1-parallel</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, azure-deployment, deploy</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Draft the coordinated CI change H2a's ARM SDK port (task 123) needs: a workflow step (or a small new workflow) that runs `az bicep build` against infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep (or the specific stamp templates H2a deploys), producing ARM JSON as a versioned build artifact H2a's handler downloads and passes to Azure.ResourceManager.Resources.ArmDeploymentResource.CreateOrUpdateAsync at provision time -- because the ARM SDK deploys ARM JSON, not raw .bicep, and the L2 runtime has no `bicep` CLI/binary available under Option D's zero-shell constraint.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in az bicep build artifact pipelines and coordinating small additive CI steps across worktree ownership boundaries.</role>

  <goal>A coordination note + drafted YAML step exists that runs az bicep build against the customer-stamp Bicep template(s) H2a deploys, uploads the resulting ARM JSON as a versioned artifact (blob or GitHub Actions artifact, matching whichever store task 116 establishes for consistency), consumable by H2a's handler-side ArmDeploymentResource.CreateOrUpdateAsync call (task 123).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-1b §1 (H2a collaborator #5) flags this as a hard caveat on H2a's ARM SDK port: 'the ARM SDK deploys ARM JSON, not .bicep -- CI pre-compiles customer.bicep -&gt; JSON artifact (one workflow step), or bundle the self-contained bicep binary.' DS-4 §4 explicitly lists this CI coordination as part of Wave G-1's foundation content, opened alongside the H9 artifact-publish coordination (task 116).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/h2a-bicep-precompile-ci-coord-pr.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="DS-1b §1 H2a row">The ARM SDK path is chosen over bundling a self-contained bicep binary into the L2 runtime, to preserve Option D's zero-shell/zero-extra-binary constraint on the main site -- do NOT propose bundling the bicep CLI as an alternative in this task's draft.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Three-question component-justification gate applies to any NEW class/interface/Bicep resource/script this task introduces. Existing/Extension/Cost-of-doing-nothing are pre-answered in &lt;notes&gt; below; cite them verbatim in the PR description per root CLAUDE.md §11 enforcement table.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>H2a Bicep-&gt;ARM-JSON CI pre-compile</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds1b-option-d-hybrid-deep-dive.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (STANDARD). Read DS-1b §1 H2a row + DS-4 §4 Wave G-1 content.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Identify template scope">Confirm exactly which Bicep template(s) H2a deploys at provision time (customer.bicep and any stack variants per Model 1/Model 2) -- the pre-compile step must cover all of them.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Draft compile step">az bicep build &lt;template&gt; --outfile &lt;name&gt;.json for each identified template; upload as a versioned artifact consistent with task 116's storage choice (reuse the SAME provisioning-artifacts container if that keeps the consumption story simple for H2a's handler).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Versioning">Tie the ARM-JSON artifact's version to the same git-sha/semver scheme task 116 establishes, so H2a's handler can resolve-by-buildId analogously to H9.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Coordination note">Author notes/h2a-bicep-precompile-ci-coord-pr.md with the drafted step, addressed to the workflow owner.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the customer-stamp Bicep templates include modules/child-resources that az bicep build cannot fully flatten into a single ARM-JSON artifact (e.g., a module referencing a template spec by id rather than inline), STOP and escalate to task 123's owner — this determines whether H2a's ARM SDK deployment call needs a nested-template strategy, which changes the handler design, not just the CI step.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="az bicep">build (local verification of the drafted step)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="infra">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/h2a-bicep-precompile-ci-coord-pr.md (contains the drafted workflow step)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A coordination note exists with the drafted az bicep build step covering every Bicep template H2a deploys.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The drafted artifact versioning scheme matches task 116's established scheme (same storage container/versioning convention) for consumption-story consistency.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Local az bicep build against the identified template(s) succeeds with 0 errors as a pre-authoring sanity check (documented in this task's notes).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- az bicep build already exists as a CLI capability; no new tooling to invent. Extension -- adding one CI step reusing an existing az CLI capability is strictly simpler than the rejected alternative (bundling the bicep binary into L2's runtime, which DS-1b's zero-shell constraint forbids). Cost-of-doing-nothing -- H2a's ARM SDK port (task 123) has no artifact to deploy; Azure.ResourceManager.Resources cannot accept raw .bicep source.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
